From: Gabe Rowe <gaber@valvesoftware.com>
Subject: [PATCH] llcc-qcom: gpu LLC priority/size increased, decrease cpuss
 max capacity

SM8650 slice table: LLCC_GPU max_cap 3096 -> 4096 KiB and priority
1 -> 2; LLCC_CPUSS max_cap 5120 -> 1024 KiB. Both slices keep
bonus_ways = 0xffffff and are not fixed_size, so each can still borrow
free ways past its cap.

Taken from the Steam Frame kernel's sm8650-7.2 branch (2fb051b4e); the
original carries no message beyond its subject and no sign-off. Carried
as an A/B TEST: on the current table the FIT's GPU already reads at
~400 GB/s up to 8 MiB (past its 3 MiB cap), and the CPU shows no clear
system-cache step between L3 and DRAM. Drop it unless the A/B shows a
gain.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
index 733999867..e90db5079 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
@@ -3394,7 +3394,7 @@ static const struct llcc_slice_config sm8650_data[] = {
 	{
 		.usecase_id = LLCC_CPUSS,
 		.slice_id = 1,
-		.max_cap = 5120,
+		.max_cap = 1024,
 		.priority = 1,
 		.bonus_ways = 0xffffff,
 		.cache_mode = 0,
@@ -3450,8 +3450,8 @@ static const struct llcc_slice_config sm8650_data[] = {
 	}, {
 		.usecase_id = LLCC_GPU,
 		.slice_id = 9,
-		.max_cap = 3096,
-		.priority = 1,
+		.max_cap = 4096,
+		.priority = 2,
 		.bonus_ways = 0xffffff,
 		.cache_mode = 0,
 		.write_scid_en = true,
